y: `OLD` over the six files prints nothing and `AMSC` prints `all comparable mirrors in sync`.\n97: - [x] T010 [P] Lane A. Point the corpus rows at the new name (`CORPUS`). For `cmd-create-skill-typed-01` and `sv-07`, check that each `split` is not `holdout`, then replace `/create:skill` with `/create:sk-skill` in `prompt` and set `expected_command` to `/create:sk-skill`. For `cmd-create-skill-plain-tune-01`, check that its `split` is `tune`, then set `expected_command` only. For the one holdout row, change only `expected_command`, with one scripted substitution that never reads or prints a prompt: `sed -i '' -E '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ s#\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"#\"expected_command\":\"/create:sk-skill\"#' $CORPUS`, and report only the count, from `awk '/\"split\":\"holdout\"/ && /\"expected_command\":\"\\/create:sk-skill\"/ {n++} END {print n+0}' $CORPUS`. Row ids stay. Verify: the `awk` count prints 1, `rg -c '\"expected_command\":\"/create:skill\"' $CORPUS` prints nothing, `jq -c 'select(.expected_command == \"/create:sk-skill\") | [.split, .row_type]' $CORPUS | sort | uniq -c` prints the four pairs of `spec.md` section 2, every line parses with `jq -c . $CORPUS > /dev/null` and `G diff --numstat HEAD -- $CORPUS` prints `4`, `4` and the path.\n98: - [x] T011 [P] Lane B. Read a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor problem cue (`HO`, `HOT`, `HCT`). In the first alternative of `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE`, inside the verb group and right after `converg\\\\w*`, add `|show(?:s|ing)? up|appear(?:s|ing)?`. In the comment above the two cue lists, add one sentence saying a tool or command that does not show up or appear is a wrong state, like one that is not registered or not found. In `HOT`, add `reads a tool that does not show up as a strong cue` with `the deploy button is not showing up after the update` and `my new agent isn't appearing in the picker` as `strong`, and `don't show line numbers in the diff` and `show me how the advisor ranks skills