{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794585424459,"sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","part":{"id":"prt_1d5a0724b001ZrpgtsAaW7NFKt","sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","messageID":"msg_1d5a067e4001FhzSzbu4q5fMW0","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794585426371,"sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5a07617001NxpVdZDFJq2Dkx","sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","messageID":"msg_1d5a067e4001FhzSzbu4q5fMW0","type":"tool","id":"call_7611e5876e4143f9b3c42612","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n 'DPR|phrases=|install|speckit:search|ownedSignals|intent phrases|reach' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md | head -60","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"2:title: \"Feature Specification: Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\"\n3:description: \"Claude Code lists 32 of the 44 tracked commands, because a command file named skill.md makes it read the create folder as one skill. This phase renames /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, offers /doctor:helper on a doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up, shows the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call with the request on stdin, adds intent phrases to five no-recommendation commands and keeps the brief-cost run out of the shared health log.\"\n5:  - \"claude create reach and doctor default\"\n6:  - \"phase 16 claude create reach and doctor default\"\n10:  - \"command intent phrases for doctor install setup speckit update\"\n15:# Feature Specification: Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n44:**Scope Boundary**: The rename of `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file outside `specs/`, the mirror check that counts Claude's commands, the doctor problem cue, `AGENTS.md` line 65 with its two derived copies, the intent phrases of five commands and the child environment of the brief-cost script. Generated files change only through their generators. No scorer weight, hub routing logic or renderer changes. `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `.claude/skills` link, every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served copy of the sk-doc canary fixture keep the old text.\n56:- Intent phrases for `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`, re-embedded and measured on holdout as a count.\n66:Claude Code shows 32 of the 44 tracked commands. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude read its folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, which the coordinator traced to an open upstream bug (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`) that holds for any capitalisation and on any filesystem. The only documented way out is another file name, and the mirror check hides the case behind an allowlist. A doctor prompt that says Code Mode tools are not showing up reaches no doctor command, because it carries no problem cue while four skills pass. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example passes the prompt in argv, which any local user can read from the process table. Five scored commands carry too little intent text to reach their prompts on the real embedder, which sits at holdout 3 of 44. One brief-cost run wrote 44 records into the operator's health log, which left a workspace reading a degraded rate of 1.0.\n69:Claude shows every tracked command under one name per command on every runtime, a doctor problem worded as a missing tool gets the doctor helper, the documented direct call keeps the prompt out of argv, five commands gain out-of-sample reach and a cost run leaves the health log alone.\n146:$ node $DS/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs | tail -1\n147:STATUS=OK phrases=248 bridges=36\n170:The coordinator's `\\b` search also matches `/create:skill-parent`, which stays, so 198 hits in 62 files hold 105 hits of the old name itself. The `OLDP` scan adds the colon form without a slash, the `create/skill.md` path and the bridge id `command-create-skill`, and with `--hidden` it reaches the agent copies of four runtimes. It lists 55 files:\n196:- Intent phrases. The four doctor routes keep their phrases in `trigger_phrases` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` (the routes at lines 65, 376, 626 and 758), because doctor commands have no `command-metadata.json`. `/speckit:search` keeps them in `userIntent.ownedSignals` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` (line 215). The deriver carries both into the bridges, and `skill_graph_scan` re-embeds the command vectors.\n209:- D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\n295:| Risk | The phrases also reach the lexical lanes, which segment four did not measure | A near-miss row could start offering a command | T021 recaptures the fixture baseline, whose false offers must stay 0 of 35, and T020 checks the three doctor-family floor rows |\n352:- Q1. How does Claude Code reach all 44 commands? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias. The rank 7 design changed from a managed `.claude/skills` tree with a Claude-only `create` skill to a rename, because the cause is an open upstream bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`): a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation and on any filesystem, hides its folder's other commands, and another file name is the only documented way out. The flat root mirror this plan proposed earlier is dropped.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"2:title: \"Feature Specification: Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\"\n3:description: \"Claude Code lists 32 of the 44 tracked commands, because a command file named skill.md makes it read the create folder as one skill. This phase renames /create:skill to /create:sk-skill on every runtime with no alias, offers /doctor:helper on a doctor prompt that says a tool is not showing up, shows the AGENTS.md Gate 2 call with the request on stdin, adds intent phrases to five no-recommendation commands and keeps the brief-cost run out of the shared health log.\"\n5:  - \"claude create reach and doctor default\"\n6:  - \"phase 16 claude create reach and doctor default\"\n10:  - \"command intent phrases for doctor install setup speckit update\"\n15:# Feature Specification: Phase 16: claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default\n44:**Scope Boundary**: The rename of `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file outside `specs/`, the mirror check that counts Claude's commands, the doctor problem cue, `AGENTS.md` line 65 with its two derived copies, the intent phrases of five commands and the child environment of the brief-cost script. Generated files change only through their generators. No scorer weight, hub routing logic or renderer changes. `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `.claude/skills` link, every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served copy of the sk-doc canary fixture keep the old text.\n56:- Intent phrases for `/doctor:install`, `/doctor:setup`, `/doctor:speckit`, `/doctor:update` and `/speckit:search`, re-embedded and measured on holdout as a count.\n66:Claude Code shows 32 of the 44 tracked commands. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude read its folder as one skill and hide the other commands in it, which the coordinator traced to an open upstream bug (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`) that holds for any capitalisation and on any filesystem. The only documented way out is another file name, and the mirror check hides the case behind an allowlist. A doctor prompt that says Code Mode tools are not showing up reaches no doctor command, because it carries no problem cue while four skills pass. The `AGENTS.md` Gate 2 example passes the prompt in argv, which any local user can read from the process table. Five scored commands carry too little intent text to reach their prompts on the real embedder, which sits at holdout 3 of 44. One brief-cost run wrote 44 records into the operator's health log, which left a workspace reading a degraded rate of 1.0.\n69:Claude shows every tracked command under one name per command on every runtime, a doctor problem worded as a missing tool gets the doctor helper, the documented direct call keeps the prompt out of argv, five commands gain out-of-sample reach and a cost run leaves the health log alone.\n146:$ node $DS/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs | tail -1\n147:STATUS=OK phrases=248 bridges=36\n170:The coordinator's `\\b` search also matches `/create:skill-parent`, which stays, so 198 hits in 62 files hold 105 hits of the old name itself. The `OLDP` scan adds the colon form without a slash, the `create/skill.md` path and the bridge id `command-create-skill`, and with `--hidden` it reaches the agent copies of four runtimes. It lists 55 files:\n196:- Intent phrases. The four doctor routes keep their phrases in `trigger_phrases` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` (the routes at lines 65, 376, 626 and 758), because doctor commands have no `command-metadata.json`. `/speckit:search` keeps them in `userIntent.ownedSignals` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` (line 215). The deriver carries both into the bridges, and `skill_graph_scan` re-embeds the command vectors.\n209:- D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\n295:| Risk | The phrases also reach the lexical lanes, which segment four did not measure | A near-miss row could start offering a command | T021 recaptures the fixture baseline, whose false offers must stay 0 of 35, and T020 checks the three doctor-family floor rows |\n352:- Q1. How does Claude Code reach all 44 commands? Answered by the operator on 2026-11-13: rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, matching `/doctor:sk-skill`, with no alias. The rank 7 design changed from a managed `.claude/skills` tree with a Claude-only `create` skill to a rename, because the cause is an open upstream bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`): a command file named `skill.md`, in any capitalisation and on any filesystem, hides its folder's other commands, and another file name is the only documented way out. The flat root mirror this plan proposed earlier is dropped.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n 'DPR|phrases=|install|speckit:search|ownedSignals|intent phrases|reach' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md | head -60\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794585425431,"end":1794585426371}}}}
