{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794585430917,"sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5a088f4001dDkXSvAx2oHB4c","sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","messageID":"msg_1d5a07e06001M8Su3U6gsLMB0W","type":"tool","id":"call_377ead08294d46feba2f1f62","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":40,"offset":188,"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md, lines 188-227\n188: - Collapse check. `COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST` (`$MS:39`) exempts `create/skill.md`, and `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` match the lowercase name only (`$MS:239-276`). With no file named `skill.md` the check reads 44 of 44 without an exception.\n189: - Doctor cue. `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` returns the ranking unchanged when a skill passes and the prompt has no strong cue (`$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1131-1135`). `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE` (`$ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:51-59`) has no \"show up\" or \"appear\". With a strong cue the helper is inserted after the second passing skill (`fusion.ts:975-976`), and the renderer prints it as `Also:` (`$ADV/lib/render.ts:564-569`).\n190: - Gate 2 call. The CLI reads `--json -` from stdin so a prompt stays out of argv (`$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts:391-397`). The manifest derives the gate-2 body from `AGENTS.md`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the call line into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md:35`. The new line 65 is 204 bytes, 16 more than today:\n191: \n192: ```text\n193: 2. B) Direct call: run `printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n194: ```\n195: \n196: - Intent phrases. The four doctor routes keep their phrases in `trigger_phrases` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` (the routes at lines 65, 376, 626 and 758), because doctor commands have no `command-metadata.json`. `/speckit:search` keeps them in `userIntent.ownedSignals` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` (line 215). The deriver carries both into the bridges, and `skill_graph_scan` re-embeds the command vectors.\n197: - Brief cost. The hook child inherits the parent's `TMPDIR` (`measure-brief-cost.mjs:167`), and the metrics root is `tmpdir()` plus a fixed folder (`metrics.ts:185`), so a cost run writes into the shared health log. Setting `TMPDIR` to the sandbox folder the script already deletes moves those records into the sandbox.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n203: ## 3. SCOPE\n204: \n205: ### In Scope\n206: - A. Rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file, with generated files rewritten by their generators, and drop the collapse allowlist from the mirror check.\n207: - B. Read a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor problem cue.\n208: - C. Show the Gate 2 direct call with the request on stdin in `AGENTS.md`, and regenerate its two copies.\n209: - D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\n210: - E. Run the brief-cost hook children with `TMPDIR` in the sandbox.\n211: - F. Regenerate the mirrors, rebuild, re-embed, recapture the baselines and check Claude's listing.\n212: \n213: ### Out of Scope\n214: - An alias for `/create:skill`. The operator chose a clean break.\n215: - `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `create-skill` mode id and the `create-skill-*` asset file names. They are not the command name a reader types.\n216: - Every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served canary fixture.\n217: - The other argv calls of the advisor CLI. The review finding names `AGENTS.md:65` only.\n218: - Segment four ranks 3 to 9. Ranks 3 and 4 wait on the operator and ranks 5 to 9 are declined there.\n219: - Starting a model session, a daemon or Ollama from a worker task.\n220: \n221: ### Files to Change\n222: \n223: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n224: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n225: | `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | Rename | Coordinator `git mv`, then its text |\n226: | The other 36 hand-edited files of the rename inventory, the mirror check files below among them | Modify | The old name to the new one, grouped by area in T004 to T010 and T014 |\n227: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, its test and its README | Modify | No allowlist, any capitalisation |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 228]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md, lines 188-227\n188: - Collapse check. `COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST` (`$MS:39`) exempts `create/skill.md`, and `commandVisibility` and `collapseDrift` match the lowercase name only (`$MS:239-276`). With no file named `skill.md` the check reads 44 of 44 without an exception.\n189: - Doctor cue. `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` returns the ranking unchanged when a skill passes and the prompt has no strong cue (`$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1131-1135`). `STRONG_PROBLEM_CUE` (`$ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:51-59`) has no \"show up\" or \"appear\". With a strong cue the helper is inserted after the second passing skill (`fusion.ts:975-976`), and the renderer prints it as `Also:` (`$ADV/lib/render.ts:564-569`).\n190: - Gate 2 call. The CLI reads `--json -` from stdin so a prompt stays out of argv (`$ADV/skill-advisor-cli.ts:391-397`). The manifest derives the gate-2 body from `AGENTS.md`, and `sync-gate1-pointers.cjs` copies the call line into `.cursor/rules/skill-routing.md:35`. The new line 65 is 204 bytes, 16 more than today:\n191: \n192: ```text\n193: 2. B) Direct call: run `printf '%s' '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' | node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n194: ```\n195: \n196: - Intent phrases. The four doctor routes keep their phrases in `trigger_phrases` in `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` (the routes at lines 65, 376, 626 and 758), because doctor commands have no `command-metadata.json`. `/speckit:search` keeps them in `userIntent.ownedSignals` in `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` (line 215). The deriver carries both into the bridges, and `skill_graph_scan` re-embeds the command vectors.\n197: - Brief cost. The hook child inherits the parent's `TMPDIR` (`measure-brief-cost.mjs:167`), and the metrics root is `tmpdir()` plus a fixed folder (`metrics.ts:185`), so a cost run writes into the shared health log. Setting `TMPDIR` to the sandbox folder the script already deletes moves those records into the sandbox.\n198: <!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n199: \n200: ---\n201: \n202: <!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n203: ## 3. SCOPE\n204: \n205: ### In Scope\n206: - A. Rename `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` in every live file, with generated files rewritten by their generators, and drop the collapse allowlist from the mirror check.\n207: - B. Read a negated \"show up\" or \"appear\" as a strong doctor problem cue.\n208: - C. Show the Gate 2 direct call with the request on stdin in `AGENTS.md`, and regenerate its two copies.\n209: - D. Add intent phrases to five commands, paraphrasing any phrase that repeats a tune prompt, re-embed and measure holdout as a count.\n210: - E. Run the brief-cost hook children with `TMPDIR` in the sandbox.\n211: - F. Regenerate the mirrors, rebuild, re-embed, recapture the baselines and check Claude's listing.\n212: \n213: ### Out of Scope\n214: - An alias for `/create:skill`. The operator chose a clean break.\n215: - `/create:skill-parent`, the `sk-create-skill` mode and its folder, the `create-skill` mode id and the `create-skill-*` asset file names. They are not the command name a reader types.\n216: - Every file under `specs/`, every published changelog entry, the dated benchmark reports and the served canary fixture.\n217: - The other argv calls of the advisor CLI. The review finding names `AGENTS.md:65` only.\n218: - Segment four ranks 3 to 9. Ranks 3 and 4 wait on the operator and ranks 5 to 9 are declined there.\n219: - Starting a model session, a daemon or Ollama from a worker task.\n220: \n221: ### Files to Change\n222: \n223: | File Path | Change Type | Description |\n224: |-----------|-------------|-------------|\n225: | `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` to `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md` | Rename | Coordinator `git mv`, then its text |\n226: | The other 36 hand-edited files of the rename inventory, the mirror check files below among them | Modify | The old name to the new one, grouped by area in T004 to T010 and T014 |\n227: | `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, its test and its README | Modify | No allowlist, any capitalisation |\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 228]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\":40,\"offset\":188,\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794585430260,"end":1794585430917}}}}
