{"type":"text","timestamp":1794585676425,"sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","part":{"id":"prt_1d5a430cd002ASG2QbY4PpOqIS","sessionID":"ses_e2a62233effea9cf1XWr6LjlNB","messageID":"msg_1d5a3f05d001ap2XJlF30GneGB","type":"text","text":"T019 is complete. Here is the record.\n\n## Files written\n\nDirectly edited (the phrases T019 names):\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml` — 19 phrases appended across the four doctor routes: 5 to `/doctor:install`, 5 to `/doctor:setup`, 5 to `/doctor:speckit`, 4 to `/doctor:update`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json` — 4 phrases appended to `userIntent.ownedSignals` of `/speckit:search`\n\nWritten by `DER` (not hand-edited):\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`\n\nPhrase handling: all five corpus rows were confirmed `split: \"tune\"` before their prompts were read. None of the `/create:skill-parent` phrases were used. One phrase, `\"walk me through putting this toolkit into my own project repository\"`, exactly equalled the install tune prompt, so it was rewritten as `\"walk me through adding this toolkit to my own project repository\"`. No holdout row was read or compared.\n\n## Verify output\n\n```\n$ # normalize lowercase + collapse spaces; compare every added phrase with its command's tune prompt\n/doctor:install added=5\n/doctor:setup added=5\n/doctor:speckit added=5\n/doctor:update added=4\n/speckit:search added=5\n0\n\n$ bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh\nOK: route-validate — 32 routes validated, 11 warnings\nexit=0\n\n$ node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs | tail -1\nSTATUS=OK phrases=267 bridges=36\nexit=0\n# 267 = 248 from scratch/before.txt + the 19 doctor phrases added\n\n$ node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check\n{\n  \"status\": \"fresh\",\n  \"counts\": {\n    \"commandMetadata\": 27,\n    \"doctorRoutes\": 36,\n    \"generated\": 63,\n    \"typescriptActive\": 46,\n    \"pythonActive\": 52\n  },\n  \"changed\": []\n}\nexit=0\n\n$ jq empty .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/command-metadata.json\nexit=0\n\n$ cd .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime && npm run typecheck\n> typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTC_exit=0\n```\n\nThe full DPR report is kept at `.../016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default/scratch/dpr-after-intent-phrases.log`.\n\n## Deviation, recorded\n\n`DPR` refuses to score against a stale dist. Before the rebuild it printed:\n\n```\ndoctor-phrase-reach: @spec-kit/system-skill-advisor dist is stale (source content differs from the attested build). Rebuild with: cd .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime && npm run build\n```\n\nBecause T019's own Verify names `DPR`, I ran `npm run build` in `$ADV`. This writes only gitignored `dist` output, touches no tracked file, and the later coordinator rebuild (T020) still runs. `git status --short` confirms `dist` and the shared build output are untracked. The coordinator is the only other thing to know: `$ADV/dist` is now built from the current source.\n\n## Not done\n\n- `tasks.md` was not edited and the T019 checkbox remains unticked, as instructed.\n- Nothing else was blocked. No tests were run because T019 names none.","time":{"start":1794585669837,"end":1794585676425}}}
